1
00:00:00,960 --> 00:00:03,880
Once upon a time, there was a knight.

2
00:00:04,500 --> 00:00:08,380
The knight never faltered in his duty, no matter what it was.

3
00:00:09,060 --> 00:00:13,720
He didn't even falter when duty demanded he take the life of his lover.

4
00:00:14,620 --> 00:00:17,200
His dedication was what he took pride in.

5
00:00:18,420 --> 00:00:22,320
But the knight couldn't do anything but carry out his duty.

6
00:00:22,960 --> 00:00:27,460
And even after death, he still seeks a duty to carry out.

7
00:00:27,460 --> 00:00:32,560
They say the knight who became a ghost and now haunts this world

8
00:00:32,560 --> 00:00:38,600
holds in his hand the blood-stained sword that pierced his lover's breast.

9
00:02:25,520 --> 00:02:55,500
I don't know.

10
00:02:55,520 --> 00:03:16,520
They say that he's appeared again! The infamous and cursed ghost knight!

11
00:03:16,520 --> 00:03:19,520
Hey, Duck! What's wrong? You're all spaced out.

12
00:03:19,520 --> 00:03:24,520
Oh no, nothing's wrong. Oh, come to think of it, today is…

13
00:03:24,520 --> 00:03:29,520
Oh! The day Fakir comes back from suspension!

14
00:03:29,520 --> 00:03:33,520
Huh? I wonder just how wretched he'll look when he comes in today!

15
00:03:33,520 --> 00:03:34,520
So he's back today…

16
00:03:34,520 --> 00:03:37,520
Huh? Are you completely a Fakir girl too now?

17
00:03:37,520 --> 00:03:38,520
What?

18
00:03:38,520 --> 00:03:41,520
No, no, I'm telling you, Fakir and I aren't anything like that! We're not anything!

19
00:03:41,520 --> 00:03:46,520
But hey, if you're really that serious about the whole thing, you're my friend and I gotta support you, don't I?

20
00:03:46,520 --> 00:03:48,520
And me too! I'll support you with everything I've got!

21
00:03:48,520 --> 00:03:49,520
No, see?

22
00:03:49,520 --> 00:03:51,520
First up, the love confession!

23
00:03:51,520 --> 00:03:52,520
What's this?

24
00:03:52,520 --> 00:03:53,520
They seem a bit freaky.

25
00:03:53,520 --> 00:03:54,520
Just walk past them, don't make eye contact.

26
00:03:54,520 --> 00:03:55,520
You be careful too, Duck!

27
00:03:55,520 --> 00:03:56,520
A duck!

28
00:03:56,520 --> 00:03:57,520
You're a duck!

29
00:03:57,520 --> 00:03:58,520
What?

30
00:03:58,520 --> 00:04:17,520
I myself am a shrimp, by the way. We are here expressing our own intangible inner worlds in a more external and concrete form. And I can see your image as that of a duck.

31
00:04:17,520 --> 00:04:18,520
Right.

32
00:04:18,520 --> 00:04:21,520
So tell me, which division are you part of as a student?

33
00:04:21,520 --> 00:04:23,520
I'm in the ballet division.

34
00:04:23,520 --> 00:04:24,520
Really?

35
00:04:24,520 --> 00:04:26,520
You think she? Why don't we ask her?

36
00:04:26,520 --> 00:04:29,520
Excuse us, do you know the wonderful Muto?

37
00:04:29,520 --> 00:04:30,520
Uh, yes.

38
00:04:30,520 --> 00:04:31,520
Oh!

39
00:04:31,520 --> 00:04:36,520
Well, you see, the truth of the matter is, we've been trying to find a boy to dance ballet for us in our upcoming show.

40
00:04:36,520 --> 00:04:37,520
Uh...

41
00:04:37,520 --> 00:04:40,520
We'd really love to ask the wonderful Muto to do it, but...

42
00:04:40,520 --> 00:04:42,520
Ask Muto?

43
00:04:42,520 --> 00:04:45,520
As proof, then, you'll give me your beautiful heart.

44
00:04:45,520 --> 00:04:48,520
No, Muto as he is now.

45
00:04:48,520 --> 00:04:52,520
Oh, um, would it be okay if Fakir did it?

46
00:04:52,520 --> 00:04:54,520
Huh? He's so scary.

47
00:04:54,520 --> 00:04:57,520
He's the guy that pushes people he doesn't like out the window, right?

48
00:04:57,520 --> 00:05:02,520
No, that's a big fat lie. And he's just as good at ballet as Muto is, so...

49
00:05:02,520 --> 00:05:05,520
That's true. As things stand, we could use Senior Fakir.

50
00:05:05,520 --> 00:05:06,520
What? Really?

51
00:05:06,520 --> 00:05:12,520
Here you go. This is a copy of the script. Could you give it to Senior Fakir for us when you see him?

52
00:05:12,520 --> 00:05:13,520
Of course. Thank you.

53
00:05:13,520 --> 00:05:29,520
Hi. I'm so glad you've come back to school, Fakir. I've been waiting for you.

54
00:05:29,520 --> 00:05:33,520
Oh, Muto! Look it! Oh, my gosh!

55
00:05:33,520 --> 00:05:35,520
Why did you come back?

56
00:05:35,520 --> 00:05:40,520
I am here to protect Muto. That's all.

57
00:05:40,520 --> 00:05:47,520
Protect? How? You're a knight who couldn't even find the strength to die. What can you do?

58
00:05:47,520 --> 00:05:51,520
The knight's role in the story was to be torn in two and die.

59
00:05:51,520 --> 00:05:56,520
But not only were you saved in that unseemly way, you've got the nerve to still be alive.

60
00:05:56,520 --> 00:06:05,520
The story no longer has need of you. Now you'll just fade away and be forgotten.

61
00:06:05,520 --> 00:06:08,520
Welcome back, Fakir. It's good to see you.

62
00:06:08,520 --> 00:06:11,520
Wonder what kind of play it is.

63
00:06:11,520 --> 00:06:15,520
Oh, Fakir! Good morning, Fakir!

64
00:06:15,520 --> 00:06:17,520
This is early for you.

65
00:06:17,520 --> 00:06:22,520
Hey, do you like plays, Fakir? Ballet is dancing, but there's stories to it and stuff too, you know?

66
00:06:22,520 --> 00:06:24,520
So it's kinda sorta like a play. I mean...

67
00:06:24,520 --> 00:06:25,520
Spit it out.

68
00:06:25,520 --> 00:06:31,520
Well, you see, the people from the drama club say they want you to dance to ballet in this play they're gonna be putting on soon.

69
00:06:31,520 --> 00:06:34,520
So read this script, okay?

70
00:06:34,520 --> 00:06:39,520
Cause if you enter the clubs and stuff, you got all the more reason to come to school, right?

71
00:06:39,520 --> 00:06:44,520
Right now, I want you to stick to Muto as close as you can, so that way...

72
00:06:44,520 --> 00:06:45,520
Um, Fakir?

73
00:06:45,520 --> 00:06:48,520
I don't need you to direct me.

74
00:06:48,520 --> 00:06:50,520
Hey, I'll leave it to you then.

75
00:06:50,520 --> 00:06:52,520
Hey, wait!

76
00:06:55,520 --> 00:06:58,520
Mr. Fakir?

77
00:06:58,520 --> 00:07:00,520
Mr. Cat?

78
00:07:00,520 --> 00:07:06,520
Bad blood between people eventually goes away, even when you're not consumed by worry.

79
00:07:06,520 --> 00:07:07,520
Oh!

80
00:07:07,520 --> 00:07:09,520
Are you doing a club activity?

81
00:07:09,520 --> 00:07:11,520
That's excellent!

82
00:07:11,520 --> 00:07:21,520
Boys and girls sweating youthful sweat together, working towards one goal, and from that comes a new meeting, and eventually love blooms, and marriage, and...

83
00:07:21,520 --> 00:07:28,520
Anyway, it's important to have the desire for a positive involvement in something.

84
00:07:28,520 --> 00:07:30,520
Mr. Cat, wait.

85
00:07:30,520 --> 00:07:31,520
Yes, Fakir?

86
00:07:31,520 --> 00:07:35,520
Do you think it's possible to turn a love that's been made impure back to normal?

87
00:07:35,520 --> 00:07:38,520
You raise a rather thorny issue.

88
00:07:38,520 --> 00:07:41,520
What is it that defines an impure love?

89
00:07:41,520 --> 00:07:45,520
After all, who can say that Odile's love is impure?

90
00:07:45,520 --> 00:07:46,520
What do you mean?

91
00:07:54,520 --> 00:07:55,520
This is...

92
00:07:55,520 --> 00:07:58,520
I wonder if Fakir read the script?

93
00:07:58,520 --> 00:07:59,520
Huh.

94
00:07:59,520 --> 00:08:00,520
Is this the place?

95
00:08:01,520 --> 00:08:02,520
Hello in there!

96
00:08:03,520 --> 00:08:04,520
Is there anybody in here?

97
00:08:05,520 --> 00:08:08,520
Maybe Fakir is... not here.

98
00:08:10,520 --> 00:08:11,520
Hey!

99
00:08:11,520 --> 00:08:12,520
Quack!

100
00:08:13,520 --> 00:08:14,520
Fakir!

101
00:08:14,520 --> 00:08:15,520
You came after all!

102
00:08:15,520 --> 00:08:17,520
Would you mind telling me where the rest of this script is?

103
00:08:17,520 --> 00:08:19,520
What do you mean the rest?

104
00:08:19,520 --> 00:08:21,520
The script cuts off right in the middle.

105
00:08:21,520 --> 00:08:22,520
It cuts off?

106
00:08:22,520 --> 00:08:23,520
What?

107
00:08:23,520 --> 00:08:28,520
So what you're saying is you dumped a script you hadn't even read on me?

108
00:08:28,520 --> 00:08:32,520
But everybody kept saying how the part was totally perfect for you and stuff!

109
00:08:32,520 --> 00:08:35,520
A ghost knight is perfect for me, huh?

110
00:08:35,520 --> 00:08:37,520
It's about a ghost knight?

111
00:08:37,520 --> 00:08:39,520
What kind of story is it?

112
00:08:40,520 --> 00:08:43,520
He was hailed as the strongest of knights.

113
00:08:43,520 --> 00:08:45,520
Enemy nations feared him.

114
00:08:45,520 --> 00:08:49,520
The knight believed his duty was to risk his life to protect his king.

115
00:08:49,520 --> 00:08:56,520
He even killed his own lover who was a spy for an enemy kingdom without faltering.

116
00:08:57,520 --> 00:08:59,520
Eventually the two nations made peace.

117
00:08:59,520 --> 00:09:01,520
But the knight was cast into exile.

118
00:09:01,520 --> 00:09:05,520
And thenceforth knew neither whom to protect nor whom to defeat.

119
00:09:05,520 --> 00:09:09,520
He died that way, his soul cursed to wander this world.

120
00:09:10,520 --> 00:09:12,520
It's at this point where the script cuts off.

121
00:09:12,520 --> 00:09:15,520
That's kind of a sad story, don't you think?

122
00:09:16,520 --> 00:09:18,520
Oh no, I think it's a riot.

123
00:09:18,520 --> 00:09:19,520
Roo!

124
00:09:19,520 --> 00:09:21,520
A wandering knight unable to do anything?

125
00:09:21,520 --> 00:09:24,520
I think the role fits you to a T, Fakir.

126
00:09:25,520 --> 00:09:27,520
Roo, wait!

127
00:09:28,520 --> 00:09:29,520
Where'd she go?

128
00:09:29,520 --> 00:09:31,520
Oh, it's Miss Duck.

129
00:09:31,520 --> 00:09:33,520
Um, Fakir is...

130
00:09:33,520 --> 00:09:36,520
Wow, you really brought her along?

131
00:09:36,520 --> 00:09:37,520
This is the original.

132
00:09:37,520 --> 00:09:49,520
To the best of our knowledge, there's no record of when the play was written or by whom.

133
00:09:49,520 --> 00:09:56,520
I happened to come across the script while I was cleaning the room.

134
00:09:57,520 --> 00:10:01,520
It was sitting inside this beat up old bag.

135
00:10:01,520 --> 00:10:04,520
After that was when the strange rumors started floating around.

136
00:10:04,520 --> 00:10:05,520
About the ghost knight.

137
00:10:05,520 --> 00:10:08,520
Of course it was impossible for a story to come true like that.

138
00:10:08,520 --> 00:10:12,520
But it certainly makes good advertising for our play, doesn't it?

139
00:10:13,520 --> 00:10:16,520
So all I have to do is dance the role of that ghost knight, correct?

140
00:10:17,520 --> 00:10:19,520
So you're really going to help us then, Senior Fakir?

141
00:10:19,520 --> 00:10:22,520
All right, Fakir, break a leg.

142
00:10:24,520 --> 00:10:26,520
Uh, hey, Fakir.

143
00:10:30,520 --> 00:10:31,520
What is it?

144
00:10:31,520 --> 00:10:34,520
What is it about this story that bothers me so much?

145
00:10:35,520 --> 00:10:37,520
And that dream I had.

146
00:10:37,520 --> 00:10:39,520
What the hell was it supposed?

147
00:10:39,520 --> 00:10:41,520
Fakir was acting strange.

148
00:10:42,520 --> 00:10:43,520
I wonder what was wrong.

149
00:10:44,520 --> 00:10:45,520
Well, whatever.

150
00:10:45,520 --> 00:10:49,520
He decided to do the play, so I should be happy about that, right?

151
00:10:50,520 --> 00:10:54,520
But you know, I wonder if there's anything else I can do for Muto.

152
00:10:55,520 --> 00:10:58,520
Or is searching for his heart shards really the only thing that I can do?

153
00:10:59,520 --> 00:11:01,520
That's right, that's right.

154
00:11:02,520 --> 00:11:06,520
You mustn't forget that, dear little duck, dear pathetic Tutu.

155
00:11:07,520 --> 00:11:11,520
Lest you be abandoned by the story, lest you be forgotten.

156
00:11:15,520 --> 00:11:20,520
What is it that�니다?

157
00:11:20,520 --> 00:11:22,520
tunnel into a Kingdom

158
00:11:27,520 --> 00:11:29,520
The opening coming of Doom Kana is crashing down.

159
00:11:30,520 --> 00:11:31,520
Would you care for some water, father?

160
00:11:32,520 --> 00:11:33,520
flames

161
00:11:34,520 --> 00:11:35,520
Where is the heart?

162
00:11:35,520 --> 00:11:43,060
Where is the heart?

163
00:11:43,560 --> 00:11:46,480
Hurry up and bring me a heart to eat.

164
00:11:46,620 --> 00:11:47,900
I'm so sorry, Father.

165
00:11:48,380 --> 00:11:51,640
I tried hard to capture you a sacrifice in the Prince's place.

166
00:11:51,820 --> 00:11:52,540
You did?

167
00:11:53,120 --> 00:11:54,580
Yes, but Father...

168
00:11:54,580 --> 00:11:55,720
What a waste.

169
00:11:56,140 --> 00:11:59,940
You will not be loved by anyone but me and the Prince in the story.

170
00:12:00,400 --> 00:12:02,240
Do you understand me, daughter?

171
00:12:02,240 --> 00:12:06,280
And there is no way that you will ever be loved so much

172
00:12:06,280 --> 00:12:09,460
that someone would forfeit his own life for you.

173
00:12:09,880 --> 00:12:11,240
Remember that well.

174
00:12:11,260 --> 00:12:11,560
Yes.

175
00:12:12,040 --> 00:12:16,740
If you stand in the Prince's way again, you will lose even my love.

176
00:12:16,800 --> 00:12:19,000
I'm sorry. I'll do things right next time.

177
00:12:27,180 --> 00:12:30,300
The Ghost Knight and that dream and now this book.

178
00:12:30,300 --> 00:12:32,380
Just what do they...

179
00:12:32,380 --> 00:12:33,680
Oh, there you are.

180
00:12:34,260 --> 00:12:35,760
Everybody's assembled already.

181
00:12:35,940 --> 00:12:37,260
Yes, I'll be right there.

182
00:12:40,960 --> 00:12:43,160
Why would I dream about the Ghost Knight?

183
00:12:43,560 --> 00:12:43,980
Why?

184
00:12:47,980 --> 00:12:50,080
Did the Ghost Knight send me that dream?

185
00:12:53,020 --> 00:12:56,240
The Knight who's lost sight of the place where he can rest his soul.

186
00:12:56,680 --> 00:12:58,180
Is he seeking something from me?

187
00:12:58,180 --> 00:13:02,980
Does he want me to give him a place to put his soul to rest?

188
00:13:03,980 --> 00:13:04,380
No.

189
00:13:04,720 --> 00:13:06,780
Maybe he's preparing a place for me to die.

190
00:13:08,400 --> 00:13:09,840
It's almost kind of scary.

191
00:13:10,400 --> 00:13:12,540
It's as if he were the real Ghost Knight.

192
00:13:12,880 --> 00:13:14,220
I'm going out shopping.

193
00:13:14,580 --> 00:13:15,380
Be back soon.

194
00:13:15,520 --> 00:13:17,120
I think I'd probably be faster.

195
00:13:17,280 --> 00:13:18,180
Want me to go instead?

196
00:13:18,680 --> 00:13:19,240
Would you?

197
00:13:19,620 --> 00:13:20,760
Then please buy these.

198
00:13:20,800 --> 00:13:21,140
Got it.

199
00:13:21,140 --> 00:13:24,760
Okay, I didn't forget anything, did I?

200
00:13:25,220 --> 00:13:27,880
But the town kind of feels a little quieter than usual.

201
00:13:28,140 --> 00:13:30,840
Probably because of all the Ghost Knight rumors now.

202
00:13:32,400 --> 00:13:33,740
I better hurry back.

203
00:13:33,740 --> 00:13:46,860
Wow, that was marvelous.

204
00:13:46,860 --> 00:13:50,140
I have complete confidence that this play will be a success.

205
00:13:51,140 --> 00:13:52,360
Wow, it's so beautiful.

206
00:13:52,360 --> 00:13:53,520
Where's Doc?

207
00:13:53,980 --> 00:13:56,040
I had her go do some shopping for me.

208
00:13:56,400 --> 00:13:56,900
I see.

209
00:13:59,660 --> 00:14:00,820
So what do you say?

210
00:14:01,000 --> 00:14:04,460
Would you do us the honor of formally becoming a member of our club, Senior Fakir?

211
00:14:04,800 --> 00:14:06,700
I just remembered something I have to do.

212
00:14:07,540 --> 00:14:08,920
Wait, Senior Fakir!

213
00:14:09,500 --> 00:14:12,200
Looks like you can't hope for much from him after all.

214
00:14:12,200 --> 00:14:17,200
Your hair is quite lovely.

215
00:14:18,060 --> 00:14:19,460
It's just like crow's feathers.

216
00:14:21,040 --> 00:14:22,160
Well, thank you.

217
00:14:22,660 --> 00:14:25,600
So tell me, have you decided on the next sacrifice yet?

218
00:14:25,980 --> 00:14:29,920
Only the ones who possess young and beautiful hearts are worthy of sacrifice.

219
00:14:30,480 --> 00:14:32,160
I have to take my time, you know.

220
00:14:32,940 --> 00:14:33,240
Oh.

221
00:14:33,840 --> 00:14:34,900
Getting impatient.

222
00:14:36,680 --> 00:14:38,900
There have been some interesting rumors lately.

223
00:14:39,160 --> 00:14:40,660
Yes, the Ghost Knight.

224
00:14:40,660 --> 00:14:42,460
Nothing escapes you, does it?

225
00:14:42,740 --> 00:14:44,280
Now that your heart's coming back.

226
00:14:45,900 --> 00:14:47,760
Princes need strong knights.

227
00:14:48,660 --> 00:14:51,620
What if you got the famous Ghost Knight on your side?

228
00:14:51,960 --> 00:14:52,560
Good idea.

229
00:14:53,080 --> 00:14:55,800
After all, you haven't been able to do anything, Crahi.

230
00:14:56,560 --> 00:14:57,620
Don't get angry.

231
00:14:58,040 --> 00:14:59,360
It's the truth, isn't it?

232
00:15:01,960 --> 00:15:05,060
In any case, I'll take your advice, Crahi.

233
00:15:05,920 --> 00:15:07,820
Why am I getting this ill feeling in?

234
00:15:08,240 --> 00:15:09,120
Is it that script?

235
00:15:09,120 --> 00:15:12,480
Or do I have the Ghost Knight to thank for this?

236
00:15:17,680 --> 00:15:19,140
This is kind of creepy.

237
00:15:19,480 --> 00:15:22,400
Hey, where did this town have a forest like this?

238
00:15:26,120 --> 00:15:27,420
It's just a horse, Duck.

239
00:15:27,500 --> 00:15:28,060
Just a horse.

240
00:15:28,160 --> 00:15:30,000
There's no such thing as the Ghost Knight, right?

241
00:15:30,100 --> 00:15:30,900
No such thing.

242
00:15:30,900 --> 00:15:31,940
Oh!

243
00:15:33,760 --> 00:15:34,620
Look!

244
00:15:35,240 --> 00:15:36,180
It's coming this way!

245
00:15:36,640 --> 00:15:37,240
No!

246
00:15:43,200 --> 00:15:43,300
Bye!

247
00:15:43,300 --> 00:15:59,680
Is that him?

248
00:15:59,680 --> 00:16:06,800
He really is, for real.

249
00:16:06,800 --> 00:16:08,200
Hang on.

250
00:16:08,200 --> 00:16:10,900
Then the ghost head.

251
00:16:10,900 --> 00:16:12,600
Not again!

252
00:16:12,600 --> 00:16:13,600
Duck!

253
00:16:13,600 --> 00:16:14,600
Is that you there?

254
00:16:14,600 --> 00:16:15,600
Oh, Fakir!

255
00:16:15,600 --> 00:16:18,600
Just now, the ghost knight!

256
00:16:18,600 --> 00:16:19,600
So you saw him?

257
00:16:19,600 --> 00:16:20,600
Yeah.

258
00:16:20,600 --> 00:16:21,600
And I think...

259
00:16:21,600 --> 00:16:24,600
I think he might be carrying a shard of Muto's heart with him.

260
00:16:24,600 --> 00:16:25,600
What?

261
00:16:25,600 --> 00:16:26,600
I see.

262
00:16:26,600 --> 00:16:29,600
So he still had a duty he needed to dispatch as a knight.

263
00:16:29,600 --> 00:16:32,600
Wait, Fakir, you're not gonna fight with that knight, are you?

264
00:16:32,600 --> 00:16:33,600
I am.

265
00:16:33,600 --> 00:16:36,600
He's been seeking the enemy he's supposed to fight with.

266
00:16:36,600 --> 00:16:37,600
But you...

267
00:16:37,600 --> 00:16:41,600
After I defeat him, you just need to return the heart shard to Muto.

268
00:16:41,600 --> 00:16:46,600
If we end up dying on each other's swords, just leave me where I lie.

269
00:16:46,600 --> 00:16:47,600
Hang on!

270
00:16:47,600 --> 00:16:55,600
It would appear that horse already senses who its master should be.

271
00:16:55,600 --> 00:16:56,600
That's right.

272
00:16:56,600 --> 00:16:59,600
I can give you what you crave.

273
00:16:59,600 --> 00:17:01,600
An enemy to defeat.

274
00:17:01,600 --> 00:17:02,600
A knight.

275
00:17:02,600 --> 00:17:06,600
Your sword is seeking blood, isn't it?

276
00:17:06,600 --> 00:17:09,600
Cut down that useless excuse for a knight.

277
00:17:09,600 --> 00:17:10,600
Muto.

278
00:17:10,600 --> 00:17:14,600
Just like the tree.

279
00:17:14,600 --> 00:17:17,600
Now, if you are a true knight, do the job.

280
00:17:17,600 --> 00:17:21,600
Then you're the one who showed me the end of the story, aren't you?

281
00:17:21,600 --> 00:17:27,600
Just as you wish, I'll take this sword and plunge it through your heart.

282
00:17:27,600 --> 00:17:33,600
That way, you can be at peace.

283
00:17:33,600 --> 00:17:34,600
Oh no!

284
00:17:34,600 --> 00:17:35,600
Ah!

285
00:17:35,600 --> 00:17:36,600
Ah!

286
00:17:36,600 --> 00:17:37,600
Ah!

287
00:17:37,600 --> 00:17:38,600
Ah!

288
00:17:38,600 --> 00:17:40,600
Oh no!

289
00:17:40,600 --> 00:17:42,600
Oh no!

290
00:17:42,600 --> 00:17:44,600
Aus.

291
00:18:09,600 --> 00:18:10,400
Stark!

292
00:18:12,600 --> 00:18:14,520
What the hell are you doing?

293
00:18:16,820 --> 00:18:19,440
Please, Bakir, do not fight.

294
00:18:20,800 --> 00:18:21,760
Wait, Tutu.

295
00:18:22,460 --> 00:18:24,100
Damn it, Tutu, where are you?

296
00:18:24,720 --> 00:18:25,240
Tutu.

297
00:18:27,220 --> 00:18:29,020
Please, come and dance with me.

298
00:18:39,420 --> 00:18:41,800
Tutu, what happened? Where are you?

299
00:18:41,800 --> 00:18:42,640
Stay away!

300
00:18:49,520 --> 00:18:53,600
No matter how many times you swing your sword, your heart won't be satisfied.

301
00:18:54,320 --> 00:18:56,180
I think you've come to that realization.

302
00:18:56,800 --> 00:19:00,140
Because it's not your real heart that's inside you now.

303
00:19:00,960 --> 00:19:04,460
What do you want so badly that you took your lover's life?

304
00:19:05,120 --> 00:19:07,900
You can't stop fighting even after you've died.

305
00:19:07,900 --> 00:19:11,240
You're so sad. You suffer so much.

306
00:19:11,240 --> 00:19:13,080
You hold so much hate.

307
00:19:13,580 --> 00:19:15,160
What do you want that much?

308
00:19:15,860 --> 00:19:19,820
Is this thing truly so much more precious than a lover's life?

309
00:19:22,540 --> 00:19:26,280
Please stop this fighting and give back Muto's heart.

310
00:19:27,160 --> 00:19:29,020
Stop this and give up your sword.

311
00:19:29,020 --> 00:19:32,240
It's true that I'm from an enemy kingdom.

312
00:19:32,980 --> 00:19:35,180
But I'm not saying it for my kingdom's sake.

313
00:19:35,860 --> 00:19:37,500
I'm saying it because I love you.

314
00:19:38,180 --> 00:19:40,540
Because I don't want you to bear any more sorrow.

315
00:19:40,540 --> 00:19:53,880
That's right, your battle has been over for a long time.

316
00:19:53,880 --> 00:19:59,540
I am the feeling of pride.

317
00:20:00,220 --> 00:20:01,840
So, the feeling of pride.

318
00:20:05,220 --> 00:20:08,920
The shards of Muto's heart that I give back are making him suffer.

319
00:20:08,920 --> 00:20:13,720
But, this is the only thing that I can do for him right now.

320
00:20:16,180 --> 00:20:21,320
Right now, I'm thinking more about how I have to get all of my feelings back as soon as I can.

321
00:20:22,040 --> 00:20:24,040
With help from Princess Tutu.

322
00:20:24,760 --> 00:20:27,300
And when that's finished, I'll go back into the story.

323
00:20:27,300 --> 00:20:33,260
Yes, the pieces of Muto's heart should go back inside, Muto, where they belong.

324
00:20:34,440 --> 00:20:35,660
Right, Muto?

325
00:20:40,360 --> 00:20:41,080
Tutu!

326
00:20:43,660 --> 00:20:46,600
The Ghost Knight, was he able to die?

327
00:20:52,180 --> 00:20:53,060
It's Duck!

328
00:20:57,300 --> 00:21:19,480
Why am I so weak?

329
00:21:19,480 --> 00:21:21,800
Can my sword not even protect her?

330
00:21:27,300 --> 00:21:40,260
Now, I'm in a bind.

331
00:21:40,620 --> 00:21:44,160
There's something sinister going on that I'm not a part of.

332
00:21:44,360 --> 00:21:48,180
And every single one of my little players is utterly useless.

333
00:21:49,080 --> 00:21:52,480
Alas, if only Aiden were still here.

334
00:21:52,480 --> 00:21:54,240
Oh, what a bind.

335
00:23:25,404 --> 00:23:28,004
I wish you weren't always going around swinging swords and stuff.

336
00:23:28,084 --> 00:23:29,544
I mean, it's really dangerous, you know?

337
00:23:29,664 --> 00:23:31,464
So you think I'm incapable as a knight?

338
00:23:31,604 --> 00:23:34,624
You have raven's blood running through your veins just like I do.

339
00:23:34,744 --> 00:23:37,684
If I have you, I can become a prima ballerina, can't I?

340
00:23:37,784 --> 00:23:41,624
The feeling that has grown to the bursting point inside you, that is real love.

341
00:23:41,664 --> 00:23:43,664
Shut up! What is this real love?

342
00:23:43,804 --> 00:23:45,564
What you're seeking is false love.

343
00:23:45,784 --> 00:23:49,364
If the love I'm seeking is false love, then all the love in the world must be false.

344
00:23:49,364 --> 00:23:53,784
All you children who love stories, come gather round.

345
00:23:56,144 --> 00:23:56,584
Let's be fair!

346
00:24:12,324 --> 00:24:13,564
Let's have a look!

